                    Alina Scott, PhD
                </h1>
                
                <div class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-serif space-y-5">
                    <p>
                        I am an Educational Technology Postdoctoral fellow in the College of Liberal Arts and History Department at the University of Texas. I support faculty in COLA interested in working with digital tools and exploring new ways to engage their classes. I am curious about the implications and limitations of emerging technologies, like artificial intelligence, and the importance of building complex human skills to meet the digital moment.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        My research explores the intersection of Black and Indigenous kinship within communities in the Eastern Woodlands of the United States in the nineteenth century. I apply historical and critical archival methodologies to tell more nuanced stories of our collective past.
                    </p>
