                    <p class="text-xs text-stone-500"><em>Journal of Early American History & Archival Studies</em></p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-warmbg-100 dark:border-stone-800">
                        An examination of how 19th-century Black and Indigenous family networks utilized legal petitioning and local land registries to navigate state encroachment and assert kinship ties.
                    </p>
